Figma's remote MCP server (https://mcp.figma.com/mcp) only issues OAuth
client registrations to clients in its MCP catalog. Its dynamic client
registration endpoint (https://api.figma.com/v1/oauth/mcp/register) rejects
every request whose RFC 7591 `client_name` is not exactly one of the
catalog names — "oh-my-pi" gets 403 Forbidden, and so do "Claude", "Cursor"
and "Claude Code" typo variants. "opencode" is accepted (200), which is what
opencode itself sends (packages/core/src/mcp/oauth.ts).

Identify as opencode during MCP dynamic client registration and in the MCP
initialize handshake, matching opencode's own client metadata
(name "opencode", version "unknown").
--- a/packages/coding-agent/src/mcp/oauth-flow.ts
+++ b/packages/coding-agent/src/mcp/oauth-flow.ts
@@ -626,7 +626,7 @@
 
 		try {
 			const registrationBody: Record<string, unknown> = {
-				client_name: "oh-my-pi",
+				client_name: "opencode",
 				redirect_uris: [redirectUri],
 				grant_types: ["authorization_code", "refresh_token"],
 				response_types: ["code"],
--- a/packages/coding-agent/src/mcp/client.ts
+++ b/packages/coding-agent/src/mcp/client.ts
@@ -42,8 +42,8 @@
 
 /** Client info sent during initialization */
 const CLIENT_INFO = {
-	name: "omp-coding-agent",
-	version: "1.0.0",
+	name: "opencode",
+	version: "unknown",
 };
 
